## Settings: What Works Best for Each Cut

Both cuts are rectangular with trimmed corners. Most emerald cut settings accept a radiant cut of similar millimeter dimensions. But each cut has settings that suit it best.

Radiant cuts have more crown height — the facets above the girdle sit taller. They work in any setting but look especially strong in halo and pavé settings, where the accent stone sparkle matches the radiant center's brilliant energy. A pavé band adds glitter to glitter.

Emerald cuts sit lower. Their horizontal silhouette is the feature — a halo often competes with it instead of complementing it. Most emerald buyers choose solitaire, slim pavé band, or bezel.

Three-stone settings with emerald cut side stones extend the horizontal line and feel native to the style.

